  "repo_truth": "The fifth fresh review admitted its exact 18-path subject and returned two Required consistency findings. The parent accepted both without waiver and produced this exact 19-path remediated documentation-only subject. Active observations now copy the immutable committed lifecycle-head event order rather than ref-sorting, with an order-divergent positive and retained-head compatibility. The checklist now selects candidate 1.2 and lifecycle-validation-result 1.0 while candidate 1.0/1.1 remain historical-only. Baseline HEAD remains db503f7a96479775fe25dbb864b9379fd3e61ac8; no Rust, released record, or immutable prior evidence changed.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 19 manifest hashes, lexical order, and aggregate before review.",
    "Read the complete revised subject and independently re-review every Option 1 authority, migration, currentness, status, recovery, and API boundary, not only the fifth-review findings.",
    "Adversarially verify the order-divergent multi-observation vector, retained-head compatibility, duplicate/reordered/incomplete/excess refusals, and current candidate-version surface, while replaying all forward/rollback crash closure.",
    "Return findings first with exact file/line evidence, failure mode, smallest documentation repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, or user task hops.",
    "No Rust or implementation approval/work, released-record rewrite, immutable prior-record edit, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.",
    "Do not inherit prior conclusions; derive the whole verdict independently."
  ],
